# Securize on by default: remove phh's securize marker before rw-system.sh reads it.
# The marker survives updates, and 1.0 and 1.1 wrote it, so it is removed on every
# boot rather than simply no longer written. A user who switches Securize off still
# gets the marker back from phh-prop-handler.sh when the saved setting loads, which
# stops the faked boot state; the fingerprint copy in rw-system.sh has run by then.
# The kompakt- prefix must sort before vndk-, whose post-fs runs rw-system.sh.
on post-fs
    rm /metadata/securize_disable
